import "core"
import obsidian("artifacts/catln-planner")
import obsidian("artifacts/catln-planner/Daily/2026-01-03.md")
import obsidian("artifacts/catln-planner/Plans.md")


# Tests a /Data/Calendar/#dayPlanner over the vault running the Day Planner plugin, which
  obsidianPlanner.ct reads. A day planner is the calendar's own answer drawn as the blocks of a day,
  so it reaches what a calendar written here would and answers what it would.
  The vault is named note by note for the reason obsidianPlanner.ct names it so. What the planner
  finds is held by its golden: each block on its day and over its span, and a task with no time
  carried apart from the blocks.
#dayPlanner
main{io -> IO} -> (){IO} =
  _<- exit(val= 0)
  ()
